{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350782-desecrated-caerns-grottoes-does-this-plot-make-sense","id":1350782,"title":"Desecrated Caerns/Grottoes? Does this plot make sense?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-25T01:07:40-08:00","id":1350782,"title":"Desecrated Caerns/Grottoes? Does this plot make sense?","content":"I might be running a Game of Mage based in siattle and I had a plot hook that I thought I would run past you guys to see if it makes sense in Werewolf lore...<br /> <br /> The players aid is requested by a Dreamspeaker mage and environmentalist. While scuba diving in Puget Sound, he discovered what appears to be a node, clogged by polluted resonance. He believes that by cleaning this node, the spiritual environment of the Sound can be improved. He has been making regular dives to the site, performing rites to adjust the resonance, however in recent attempts he has been harried by massive sharks who seem to resist his magick.<br /> <br /> History: In 1978, the Technocracy, in an alliance with Pentex, sent a submarine, the USS Puffer, to the location of the node, which also happened to be a Rokea grotto. There, they dumped 500 gallons of radioactive waste &quot;by accident&quot; and brought the submarine's weapons to bear on the Weresharks, destroying them and the node. This act altered the flow of quintessence in the area, resulting in a net gain for Technocratic-owned nodes and a decrease in Tradition-owned ones.<br /> <br /> In the years since, the Rokea have been unable to undo the damage caused by the radioactive waste, and have considered the grotto lost. More recently, a wandering Rokea visited the site, and discovered signs of human tampering. This Rokea began watching the site, and due to complete mistrust of humans, has been attempting to scare away the Dreamspeaker diver. He has since called in allies. To complicate matters, Pentex has been monitoring the situation...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> One thing I am curious about is what a corrupted caern/grotto might be like. The Rokea's actions seem consistent to me, but maybe you guys might not agree. Maybe some of you might have other ideas that might spice it up or something I haven't considered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T10:46:08-08:00","id":1350856,"title":"","content":"I'd say that what you described is fairly consistent for the Rokea.<br /> <br /> The Rokea will likely want to patrol and keep the caern away from outsiders who may either spread or harness its corruption while they work on ways to cure the blight, while also naturally distrusting anything that would choose to investigate a wyrm pit.<br /> <br /> You may also want to consider having BaleSharks (Fallen Rokea) guarding the fallen grottoe as an additional twist if that interests you.<br /> <br /> What a fallen grottoe would like like honestly depends a lot upon its former spiritual nature and the nature of its corruption. One thing though, it will drive away natural life like the plague. It will corrupt and disease anything that attempts to approach it in attempts to fester and spread its malignancy. It will be a breeding ground for aquatic banes and perhaps even aquatic fomori animals. There may be wells of waste remaining that serve to spawn radioactive elementals and corrupt nearby wildlife spirits to take on radioactive elements and spread the corruption.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say... it's a Bad Time\u2122.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:05:10-08:00","id":1350872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350782-desecrated-caerns-grottoes-does-this-plot-make-sense?p=1350856#post1350856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that what you described is fairly consistent for the Rokea.<br /> <br /> The Rokea will likely want to patrol and keep the caern away from outsiders who may either spread or harness its corruption while they work on ways to cure the blight, while also naturally distrusting anything that would choose to investigate a wyrm pit.<br /> <br /> You may also want to consider having BaleSharks (Fallen Rokea) guarding the fallen grottoe as an additional twist if that interests you.<br /> <br /> What a fallen grottoe would like like honestly depends a lot upon its former spiritual nature and the nature of its corruption. One thing though, it will drive away natural life like the plague. It will corrupt and disease anything that attempts to approach it in attempts to fester and spread its malignancy. It will be a breeding ground for aquatic banes and perhaps even aquatic fomori animals. There may be wells of waste remaining that serve to spawn radioactive elementals and corrupt nearby wildlife spirits to take on radioactive elements and spread the corruption.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say... it's a Bad Time\u2122.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Pacific_garbage_patch\" target=\"_blank\">Great Pacific garbage patch</a> would be an ideal location for an extensive Wyrmish grotto network.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:11:49-08:00","id":1350875,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhhhh yeah, the Great Pacific Garbage Patch is probably a Rank 5 Wyrm grottoe or just about and likely one of the sickest hellholes (as in the Wyrmish genius loci) in 'real space'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}